# Build-context exclusions for the multi-stage Dockerfile.
#
# Two of these are correctness requirements, not just context-size savings:
#
#   config.yaml  — gitignored precisely because it holds real API keys. If it
#                  reaches the build context, `COPY . .` bakes it into a builder
#                  layer, and anyone who gets the image can read the keys back
#                  out of it. The image must never contain a config file: it is
#                  mounted at runtime (see deploy/README.md).
#   .git         — the full history can hold the same secrets, and it is usually
#                  the single largest thing in the context.
#
# vendor/ is deliberately NOT excluded: with a vendor directory present Go builds
# offline via -mod=vendor, which is the escape hatch for a network-less build
# (spec-deployment-fault-drill.md fact #2).

# --- secrets & VCS ---
config.yaml
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- local scratch: throwaway binaries, configs, audit trails, drill logs ---
.smoke/
bin/
dist/
data/
coverage.out
coverage.html
*.log
*.test
*.exe

# --- editor / tooling caches (the repowiki tree alone is larger than the source) ---
.qoder/
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
*.swp

# --- not needed to build the two binaries ---
docs/
*.md
deploy/
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
